cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SmogSense in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SmogSense: A Spatiotemporal Machine Learning Architecture for Probabilistic PM2.5 Forecasting in Sensor-Sparse Regions"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "SmogSense contributors"
keywords:
  - air quality
  - PM2.5
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - quantile regression
  - meta-learning
  - transfer learning
  - Lahore
  - Indo-Gangetic Plain
abstract: >-
  An open, zero-cost pipeline that produces daily bilingual (English/Urdu) probabilistic PM2.5 forecasts for Lahore,
  using CAMS forecasts, NASA FIRMS fire detections and few-shot transfer learning from data-rich Indo-Gangetic cities.
